1
00:00:55,247 --> 00:00:57,249
Whoever gets
to the temple first wins!

2
00:00:57,336 --> 00:00:59,642
What? Aang, no fair!

3
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:02,776
Let's get him!

4
00:01:02,863 --> 00:01:04,169
Come on, hurry up!

5
00:01:12,264 --> 00:01:13,961
Hi, Nima.
Good morning, Aang.

6
00:01:14,048 --> 00:01:15,310
Hey, Mip-Mip.
Oh, hello, Aang.

7
00:01:22,361 --> 00:01:24,058
Oh, perfect timing.
Huh?

8
00:01:24,798 --> 00:01:26,191
Mind giving me a lift?

9
00:01:26,278 --> 00:01:28,323
Gyatso, this isn't
the best time.

10
00:01:28,410 --> 00:01:30,020
I'm getting old, you know.

11
00:01:30,107 --> 00:01:32,371
My body doesn't move
like it used to.

12
00:01:32,458 --> 00:01:34,416
I'm kind of
in the middle of something.

13
00:01:34,503 --> 00:01:36,113
You are so heavy!

14
00:01:36,201 --> 00:01:39,291
Heavy? Me?
I eat nothing but vegetables.

15
00:01:39,378 --> 00:01:41,206
Pie is not a vegetable.

16
00:01:41,293 --> 00:01:42,816
I'm gonna lose the race!

17
00:01:42,903 --> 00:01:45,035
Race? What race?

18
00:01:45,122 --> 00:01:46,341
We finally won!

19
00:01:46,428 --> 00:01:47,734
We won! We won!

20
00:01:47,821 --> 00:01:49,562
Yay, we did it!

21
00:01:53,609 --> 00:01:56,308
Aang, as an Airbender,

22
00:01:56,395 --> 00:01:58,875
it's important that you know
when to show restraint.

23
00:02:00,616 --> 00:02:02,618
Even if you have
the power to win,

24
00:02:03,140 --> 00:02:04,881
you are the Avatar.

25
00:02:04,968 --> 00:02:08,798
A lot of people
are going to rely on you.

26
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,680
Where's the Avatar?

27
00:02:20,767 --> 00:02:22,421
He's gone! He ran away!

28
00:02:22,508 --> 00:02:23,813
What? I'm here!

29
00:02:24,814 --> 00:02:27,208
-Where's the Avatar?
-Avatar!

30
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:30,080
Aang! Where are you?

31
00:02:30,167 --> 00:02:31,560
Gyatso! I'm here!

32
00:02:34,781 --> 00:02:37,262
I'm... I'm... here!

33
00:02:37,349 --> 00:02:39,481
I'm here! I'm here!

34
00:02:39,568 --> 00:02:40,787
Here!

35
00:02:41,527 --> 00:02:42,702
I'm here.

36
00:02:46,836 --> 00:02:48,142
Hey, Momo.

37
00:02:49,099 --> 00:02:50,318
Hi, Appa.

38
00:02:50,405 --> 00:02:52,146
Was I asleep for long?

39
00:02:52,233 --> 00:02:54,061
Okay, okay.
I'm awake already.

40
00:02:54,148 --> 00:02:56,803
I know, I know.
We've got a job to finish.

41
00:02:57,412 --> 00:02:59,893
Let's continue our journey.

42
00:03:00,589 --> 00:03:01,764
Back to our old home.

43
00:03:50,030 --> 00:03:51,727
This may not
have been our best trip,

44
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:54,513
but any Airbender relic we find
makes it all worthwhile.

45
00:04:00,649 --> 00:04:02,695
This could be the oldest piece
in our collection.

46
00:04:08,701 --> 00:04:10,050
"Sonam."

47
00:04:22,715 --> 00:04:23,803
I miss you.

48
00:04:30,418 --> 00:04:32,551
Momo, go outside with Appa.

49
00:04:34,161 --> 00:04:35,336
Now!

50
00:04:39,558 --> 00:04:40,559
Whoa!

51
00:04:44,476 --> 00:04:46,695
Who are you?
Why are you doing this?

52
00:04:50,699 --> 00:04:53,136
Please stop.
I don't want to hurt you.

53
00:04:56,879 --> 00:04:58,533
Where is it?
Where is it?

54
00:04:58,620 --> 00:04:59,926
No, that's not it.

55
00:05:00,013 --> 00:05:01,362
Hey, those are antiques.

56
00:05:12,765 --> 00:05:13,983
Enough!

57
00:05:17,378 --> 00:05:19,859
Wait! I found it!

58
00:05:21,774 --> 00:05:23,515
Sonam? Why are they after you?

59
00:05:42,490 --> 00:05:43,360
Wait!

60
00:05:46,712 --> 00:05:49,062
No! That's a thousand years old!

61
00:05:53,632 --> 00:05:54,894
Give it to me!

62
00:05:54,981 --> 00:05:56,765
Why don't we just talk?
Maybe I can help.

63
00:05:56,852 --> 00:05:58,854
We don't need your help, Avatar.

64
00:05:59,899 --> 00:06:02,554
We're done living in a world
where Benders have all the power

65
00:06:02,641 --> 00:06:04,556
and we have none.
Who are you?

66
00:06:04,643 --> 00:06:05,687
We're the Denied.

67
00:06:05,774 --> 00:06:07,036
The Denied?

68
00:06:07,123 --> 00:06:08,516
Just kill him already!

69
00:06:08,603 --> 00:06:10,431
No! You'll bring
the whole place down!

70
00:06:37,197 --> 00:06:39,025
You... saved me.

71
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:43,246
Kallik, grab the map.
Let’s go!

72
00:06:57,565 --> 00:06:58,435
Oh, no!

73
00:07:55,057 --> 00:07:57,103
I'm fine.

74
00:07:57,190 --> 00:07:58,583
Momo, I'm fine.

75
00:08:01,673 --> 00:08:03,588
But we've got
to get to Republic City.

76
00:08:04,632 --> 00:08:06,373
Appa, yip-yip!

77
00:08:23,782 --> 00:08:24,913
<i>Water.</i>

78
00:08:25,435 --> 00:08:27,655
<i>Her tribes gather strength </i>
<i>from the moon</i>

79
00:08:28,961 --> 00:08:30,789
<i>and flow with the tides.</i>

80
00:08:32,529 --> 00:08:33,661
<i>Earth.</i>

81
00:08:33,966 --> 00:08:39,014
<i>A kingdom of unshakable will, </i>
<i>reliable and strong.</i>

82
00:08:42,627 --> 00:08:43,758
<i>Fire.</i>

83
00:08:44,454 --> 00:08:47,022
<i>A nation capable</i>
<i>of great destruction,</i>

84
00:08:48,415 --> 00:08:51,461
<i>but also of great warmth.</i>

85
00:08:53,986 --> 00:08:55,248
<i>Air.</i>

86
00:08:55,335 --> 00:08:58,077
<i>Peaceful nomads with </i>
<i>the power of a hurricane,</i>

87
00:08:58,599 --> 00:09:00,775
<i>but the spirit</i>
<i>of a gentle breeze.</i>

88
00:09:03,125 --> 00:09:05,998
<i>For generations, the Avatar,</i>

89
00:09:06,085 --> 00:09:08,827
<i>the one master</i>
<i>of all four elements,</i>

90
00:09:08,914 --> 00:09:10,916
<i>kept the nations in balance.</i>

91
00:09:12,700 --> 00:09:16,138
<i>But when that responsibility </i>
<i>fell to me as a child,</i>

92
00:09:16,225 --> 00:09:17,357
<i>I ran away.</i>

93
00:09:17,879 --> 00:09:19,838
<i>I was caught in a deadly storm,</i>

94
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:23,711
<i>but my Avatar spirit</i>
<i>preserved me</i> <i>in a sphere of energy</i>

95
00:09:23,798 --> 00:09:26,758
<i>where I stayed</i>
<i>for a hundred years.</i>

96
00:09:27,715 --> 00:09:29,064
<i>I woke to discover</i>

97
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:31,545
<i>that the balance</i>
<i>preserved by the Avatar</i>

98
00:09:31,632 --> 00:09:33,678
<i>had been destroyed by war.</i>

99
00:09:34,722 --> 00:09:36,811
<i>The Air Nomads were gone.</i>

100
00:09:37,725 --> 00:09:38,900
<i>All but one.</i>

101
00:09:39,466 --> 00:09:40,467
<i>Me.</i>

102
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:43,470
<i>I could no longer run</i>
<i>from my responsibility</i>

103
00:09:43,557 --> 00:09:44,906
<i>as the Avatar.</i>

104
00:09:45,907 --> 00:09:48,257
<i>I found allies</i>
<i>from every nation,</i>

105
00:09:48,823 --> 00:09:51,043
<i>Benders and Nonbenders.</i>

106
00:09:52,827 --> 00:09:54,960
<i>Katara taught me</i>
<i>how to waterbend.</i>

107
00:09:55,830 --> 00:09:58,528
<i>Toph trained me in the ways </i>
<i>of the Earthbenders.</i>

108
00:09:59,312 --> 00:10:03,664
<i>Zuko, once my worst enemy, </i>
<i>became my firebending teacher.</i>

109
00:10:04,665 --> 00:10:08,060
<i>Sokka showed me that bravery </i>
<i>is the most important part</i>

110
00:10:08,147 --> 00:10:09,365
<i>of being a leader.</i>

111
00:10:10,366 --> 00:10:12,194
<i>We became a family.</i>

112
00:10:13,369 --> 00:10:16,633
<i>And together, we ended</i>
<i>the Hundred Year War.</i>

113
00:10:17,983 --> 00:10:22,465
<i>Then, we began the hard work </i>
<i>of rebuilding the world.</i>

114
00:10:34,173 --> 00:10:37,002
<i>For so long,</i>
<i>the nation stood apart,</i>

115
00:10:37,089 --> 00:10:38,133
<i>alone,</i>

116
00:10:38,220 --> 00:10:40,179
<i>and we all suffered</i>
<i>as a result.</i>

117
00:10:40,266 --> 00:10:43,269
<i>But here,</i>
<i>on this ancient site,</i>

118
00:10:43,356 --> 00:10:45,662
<i>we created a place </i>
<i>where all people are welcome,</i>

119
00:10:46,359 --> 00:10:48,622
<i>Bender and Nonbender alike,</i>

120
00:10:48,709 --> 00:10:52,495
<i>working together in peace </i>
<i>to build the future.</i>

121
00:10:52,582 --> 00:10:54,846
<i>Though there are still</i>
<i>those who would seek</i>

122
00:10:54,933 --> 00:10:57,587
to divide us,
we remain united.

123
00:10:58,458 --> 00:10:59,938
As a council representative,

124
00:11:00,025 --> 00:11:02,288
I am honored
to be here today

125
00:11:02,375 --> 00:11:05,291
celebrating the anniversary
of Republic City

126
00:11:05,378 --> 00:11:07,554
and the opening
of Unity Tower,

127
00:11:07,641 --> 00:11:09,774
a symbol for all people.

128
00:11:16,345 --> 00:11:17,477
Look!

129
00:11:17,564 --> 00:11:18,783
Yeah!

130
00:11:18,870 --> 00:11:20,480
It's the Avatar!

131
00:11:23,831 --> 00:11:26,094
Whoo!
Whoo!

132
00:11:31,926 --> 00:11:33,319
Momo!

133
00:11:35,582 --> 00:11:37,323
Appa!

134
00:11:37,410 --> 00:11:39,064
I missed you too,
old friend.

135
00:11:41,283 --> 00:11:42,502
Aang!

136
00:11:42,589 --> 00:11:43,546
Katara!

137
00:11:43,633 --> 00:11:44,765
Mm!

138
00:11:48,769 --> 00:11:49,944
You're hurt.

139
00:11:57,778 --> 00:11:59,258
Take a deep breath.

140
00:12:01,521 --> 00:12:03,871
And... exhale.

141
00:12:05,264 --> 00:12:07,309
I've heard the Denied
are growing in numbers,

142
00:12:07,396 --> 00:12:09,398
but they've never
done anything like this.

143
00:12:09,485 --> 00:12:10,704
Attacking the Avatar?

144
00:12:10,791 --> 00:12:12,271
Yeah.

145
00:12:12,358 --> 00:12:13,925
They were incredible fighters.

146
00:12:14,577 --> 00:12:16,057
Even without bending.

147
00:12:18,146 --> 00:12:20,670
Oops. Breathe through it.
Ow!

148
00:12:20,757 --> 00:12:22,585
Be honest.
You're enjoying this.

149
00:12:22,672 --> 00:12:24,761
Aang, this is serious.

150
00:12:24,849 --> 00:12:26,851
Whatever this map
they took was,

151
00:12:26,938 --> 00:12:29,505
if they were willing
to kill the Avatar to get it,

152
00:12:29,592 --> 00:12:31,290
what else
are they willing to do?

153
00:12:31,899 --> 00:12:33,074
I don't know.

154
00:12:33,945 --> 00:12:35,381
I'm worried about you.

155
00:12:36,251 --> 00:12:37,687
You're spending more
and more time

156
00:12:37,774 --> 00:12:39,820
at the Air Temple, alone.

157
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:43,868
It's how I hold on to my past.

158
00:12:45,870 --> 00:12:48,002
I know how hard
this is for you.

159
00:12:52,311 --> 00:12:53,878
When I was attacked,

160
00:12:54,661 --> 00:12:56,793
all I could think about
was that...

161
00:12:57,533 --> 00:12:59,013
this could be it.

162
00:13:00,580 --> 00:13:03,017
I'm the last Airbender.

163
00:13:04,584 --> 00:13:08,370
If I die,
my culture dies with me.

164
00:13:11,460 --> 00:13:15,160
You may be the last Airbender,
but you're not alone.

165
00:13:16,074 --> 00:13:19,729
Aang, none of this
would exist without you.

166
00:13:21,166 --> 00:13:23,516
You made the city possible
with your heart

167
00:13:23,603 --> 00:13:24,821
and your mind.

168
00:13:26,519 --> 00:13:27,868
Because of you...

169
00:13:28,521 --> 00:13:30,392
all of the nations
live here...

170
00:13:30,479 --> 00:13:31,611
together.

171
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:35,223
All except mine.

172
00:13:45,407 --> 00:13:46,756
I know...

173
00:13:46,843 --> 00:13:49,324
but the people here
still need your protection.

174
00:13:50,412 --> 00:13:51,979
You're an Airbender...

175
00:13:53,024 --> 00:13:54,764
but you're also the Avatar.

176
00:13:57,115 --> 00:13:58,246
You're right.

177
00:13:59,726 --> 00:14:03,121
Whoever this Sonam person is,
I need to find out more.

178
00:14:29,060 --> 00:14:30,278
Aang.

179
00:14:30,365 --> 00:14:31,714
Avatar Roku.

180
00:14:31,801 --> 00:14:34,108
It is good
to see you again.

181
00:14:34,195 --> 00:14:35,718
How can I help you?

182
00:14:35,805 --> 00:14:37,807
In your lifetime,
did you ever hear

183
00:14:37,894 --> 00:14:40,027
of an ancient Airbender
named Sonam?

184
00:14:40,114 --> 00:14:41,507
I have not,

185
00:14:41,594 --> 00:14:44,814
but you have many
past lives to call upon.

186
00:14:44,901 --> 00:14:47,469
Perhaps one further back
in the Avatar cycle

187
00:14:47,556 --> 00:14:49,080
can help you.

188
00:14:49,645 --> 00:14:51,125
Thank you, Avatar Roku.

189
00:14:53,432 --> 00:14:55,347
I'm sorry.
I've never heard of Sonam.

190
00:14:55,434 --> 00:14:57,001
I'm unfamiliar.
Perhaps earlier.

191
00:14:57,088 --> 00:14:58,393
You must go further back.

192
00:14:58,828 --> 00:15:00,569
You must go further back. Not here.

193
00:15:00,656 --> 00:15:02,136
...in the Avatar Cycle.

194
00:15:09,056 --> 00:15:10,971
Um, hello?

195
00:15:11,885 --> 00:15:13,234
Is there anyone here?

196
00:15:14,583 --> 00:15:15,932
Hello?

197
00:15:17,978 --> 00:15:20,763
Who calls upon Avatar Xian's

198
00:15:20,850 --> 00:15:22,939
vast wealth of knowledge?

199
00:15:26,943 --> 00:15:28,467
Oh, hello.

200
00:15:28,554 --> 00:15:32,079
You look like an Avatar
from a time quite distant from mine.

201
00:15:32,166 --> 00:15:34,908
Please, please,
tell me about your era.

202
00:15:34,995 --> 00:15:36,692
What are people wearing?

203
00:15:36,779 --> 00:15:38,346
Are sandals still a thing?

204
00:15:38,433 --> 00:15:39,695
Uh, yes.

205
00:15:39,782 --> 00:15:41,219
Why?

206
00:15:41,306 --> 00:15:43,743
Why, after so many years,

207
00:15:43,830 --> 00:15:47,442
open toes, seeing someone
else's crusty cuticles?

208
00:15:47,877 --> 00:15:49,270
Disgusting!

209
00:15:49,357 --> 00:15:50,445
Right.

210
00:15:50,532 --> 00:15:52,665
Anyway, I have come
for your guidance.

211
00:15:52,752 --> 00:15:54,275
You see, I was attacked.

212
00:15:54,362 --> 00:15:56,277
It was not me, okay?
Wasn't me.

213
00:15:56,364 --> 00:15:57,539
I know that.

214
00:15:57,626 --> 00:15:58,932
I think it might have
something to do

215
00:15:59,019 --> 00:16:00,760
with an Airbender named Sonam.

216
00:16:00,847 --> 00:16:02,805
Hmm. Sonam.

217
00:16:02,892 --> 00:16:04,764
It sounds familiar.

218
00:16:04,851 --> 00:16:07,201
Sonam.
Where have I heard that name before?

219
00:16:07,288 --> 00:16:08,463
Ah-ha!

220
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,335
Sonam was the youngest daughter
of the owner

221
00:16:10,422 --> 00:16:12,554
of the possum-chicken shop
at the corner marketplace.

222
00:16:12,641 --> 00:16:15,514
Wait, that was my ex,
So Nyung.

223
00:16:15,601 --> 00:16:18,604
If only she didn't have
those humongous toenails.

224
00:16:18,691 --> 00:16:20,388
Disgusting.

225
00:16:20,475 --> 00:16:21,694
This is going nowhere.

226
00:16:21,781 --> 00:16:23,391
Sonam... So-nahm...
Sonum?

227
00:16:23,478 --> 00:16:25,872
Well,
thank you for your time.

228
00:16:25,959 --> 00:16:27,874
I must continue my search.

229
00:16:27,961 --> 00:16:30,137
Oh, Sonam!

230
00:16:30,224 --> 00:16:33,967
You're asking about the legend
of the lost Avatar.

231
00:16:34,489 --> 00:16:36,100
Sonam was an Avatar?

232
00:16:36,187 --> 00:16:37,797
Indeed she was!

233
00:16:37,884 --> 00:16:39,712
She was the Avatar

234
00:16:39,799 --> 00:16:42,584
in the golden age
of Airbenders.

235
00:16:42,671 --> 00:16:45,413
Legend said she had
a staff that could channel

236
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,373
the vast energy
of the Spirit World,

237
00:16:48,460 --> 00:16:51,680
granting its keeper
unlimited power.

238
00:16:51,767 --> 00:16:54,118
Is... Is that even possible?

239
00:16:54,988 --> 00:16:57,208
Eh, we'll never know for sure.

240
00:16:57,295 --> 00:16:59,645
Many Avatars have tried
to communicate with her,

241
00:16:59,732 --> 00:17:00,907
but they couldn't.

242
00:17:00,994 --> 00:17:02,648
She disappeared
so completely

243
00:17:02,735 --> 00:17:05,651
that it was as if
she never existed.

244
00:17:05,738 --> 00:17:07,783
And perhaps
it's better that way.

245
00:17:08,436 --> 00:17:10,830
Maybe such a staff
was too dangerous

246
00:17:10,917 --> 00:17:14,703
for anyone to possess,
even the Avatar.

247
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:17,402
But... But that's exactly
why I need to find it.

248
00:17:17,489 --> 00:17:20,013
The people who attacked me
discovered a map.

249
00:17:20,100 --> 00:17:21,667
It must lead to the staff.

250
00:17:22,233 --> 00:17:24,365
Avatar Xian, please,

251
00:17:24,452 --> 00:17:26,324
you have to tell me
where it is.

252
00:17:29,022 --> 00:17:32,634
The legend says that Sonam
disappeared with her staff

253
00:17:32,721 --> 00:17:34,897
on the peak
of Mount Baihu.

254
00:17:37,422 --> 00:17:40,381
<i>"Katara, I'm sorry</i>
<i>to leave so suddenly,</i>

255
00:17:40,468 --> 00:17:42,601
<i>but I found out </i>
<i>what the Denied are after."</i>

256
00:17:43,602 --> 00:17:45,691
<i>"Sonam had a staff</i>
<i>of immense power,</i>

257
00:17:46,300 --> 00:17:47,562
<i>and in their hands,</i>

258
00:17:47,649 --> 00:17:49,477
<i>it could be</i>
<i>a devastating weapon."</i>

259
00:17:50,348 --> 00:17:51,914
<i>"They have a head start."</i>

260
00:17:52,001 --> 00:17:53,481
<i>"There's no time to waste."</i>

261
00:17:54,656 --> 00:17:57,572
<i>"You take Appa and Momo</i>
<i>and gather up</i> <i>the rest of the team."</i>

262
00:17:57,659 --> 00:17:59,183
<i>"We're gonna need some help."</i>

263
00:18:05,798 --> 00:18:07,191
Next on the agenda,

264
00:18:07,278 --> 00:18:09,280
a Fire Nation naval vessel
came into conflict

265
00:18:09,367 --> 00:18:12,500
with an extremist group
of Nonbenders called the Denied.

266
00:18:12,587 --> 00:18:15,547
They've been
robbing ancient sites... Your Majesty! Your Majesty!

267
00:18:15,634 --> 00:18:18,071
An urgent message has arrived
from Republic City.

268
00:18:18,158 --> 00:18:19,464
How impudent.

269
00:18:19,551 --> 00:18:21,074
Can't you see
Fire Lord Zuko is...

270
00:18:21,161 --> 00:18:22,249
Chamberlain.

271
00:18:23,381 --> 00:18:25,209
There's only one person
who can send a message

272
00:18:25,296 --> 00:18:27,428
urgent enough to interrupt
the Fire Lord's counsel.

273
00:18:27,907 --> 00:18:29,822
Is it from the Avatar?
Yes, my lord.

274
00:18:29,909 --> 00:18:31,954
Read it to me.
Yes, my lord.

275
00:18:34,696 --> 00:18:36,176
Um...

276
00:18:36,263 --> 00:18:37,351
What are you doing?

277
00:18:37,438 --> 00:18:38,700
Read it quickly.

278
00:18:38,787 --> 00:18:41,050
Uh... Yeah, yeah.
Yes, Grand Chamberlain.

279
00:18:42,530 --> 00:18:45,577
"Flameo Hotman,
how's ruling the Fire Nation?"

280
00:18:45,664 --> 00:18:49,276
"I hope the boring Chamberlain
you mention in your letters

281
00:18:49,363 --> 00:18:51,800
isn't still annoying you."

282
00:18:51,887 --> 00:18:55,195
"Anyhoo, to cut to the chase,
I need your help."

283
00:18:55,282 --> 00:18:57,328
"Can you please
come immediately?"

284
00:18:57,415 --> 00:19:01,070
"Oh, and don't forget to bring
some firecracker buns."

285
00:19:03,595 --> 00:19:06,206
<i>Allow me</i>
<i>to present Sokka-Cycle.</i>

286
00:19:06,293 --> 00:19:07,816
Flames launch you into the sky

287
00:19:07,903 --> 00:19:10,515
where you can drop
water bombs on your enemies,

288
00:19:10,602 --> 00:19:13,213
then skis pop out
to help you stick the landing.

289
00:19:13,300 --> 00:19:14,736
Pretty great, right?

290
00:19:14,823 --> 00:19:16,216
Eh, boring.

291
00:19:16,303 --> 00:19:18,523
Why would you need a sled
when you can just waterbend?

292
00:19:18,610 --> 00:19:20,089
Ooh, ooh, ooh.
Like me, like me!

293
00:19:20,176 --> 00:19:21,265
Whee!

294
00:19:21,352 --> 00:19:22,570
Keep in mind,
there are still

295
00:19:22,657 --> 00:19:24,616
plenty of folks like me
who can't bend.

296
00:19:24,703 --> 00:19:27,183
Why would Avatar Aang
partner with a Nonbender?

297
00:19:27,271 --> 00:19:29,925
Why?
I'll tell you why.

298
00:19:30,012 --> 00:19:31,492
<i>I saved him from the iceberg.</i>

299
00:19:31,579 --> 00:19:33,146
<i>My boomerang flew by his side</i>

300
00:19:33,233 --> 00:19:35,670
<i>while I parried away enemies </i>
<i>with my trusty blade.</i>

301
00:19:35,757 --> 00:19:38,586
<i>I even took down the whole </i>
<i>Fire Nation airship armada.</i>

302
00:19:40,762 --> 00:19:42,155
<i>And on top of all that,</i>

303
00:19:42,242 --> 00:19:43,852
<i>I was more popular than him.</i>

304
00:19:45,201 --> 00:19:46,681
You're such a liar, Sokka.

305
00:19:49,945 --> 00:19:51,120
It's from the Avatar.

306
00:19:51,207 --> 00:19:52,948
Wow.Really?
That's so cool!

307
00:19:53,035 --> 00:19:54,863
Oh, so now
you think I'm cool?

308
00:19:56,082 --> 00:19:58,214
<i>All right, Metalbenders.</i>

309
00:19:58,302 --> 00:20:00,391
Let's see if
any of you tenderfoots

310
00:20:00,478 --> 00:20:01,957
can at least make me
use my hands.

311
00:20:35,339 --> 00:20:38,080
I'm still the greatest
Earthbender in the world!

312
00:20:39,517 --> 00:20:40,735
And I'm bored.

313
00:20:41,388 --> 00:20:43,912
Master Toph,
there's a bird on your head.

314
00:20:43,999 --> 00:20:46,219
And?
It looks like it has a message.

315
00:20:46,306 --> 00:20:47,351
Read.

316
00:20:47,655 --> 00:20:50,528
Uh, it's from Avatar Aang.
He needs your help.

317
00:20:50,615 --> 00:20:51,964
It's the Denied?
The Denied?

318
00:20:52,051 --> 00:20:53,139
Where is he?

319
00:20:53,226 --> 00:20:54,836
Mount Baihu.

320
00:21:57,116 --> 00:21:58,770
No, no, no!

321
00:21:58,857 --> 00:22:00,119
No!

322
00:22:03,862 --> 00:22:05,472
I love that hat.

323
00:23:49,968 --> 00:23:51,273
Sonam?

324
00:23:56,191 --> 00:23:57,715
Could that be you?

325
00:25:01,039 --> 00:25:02,388
Who are you?

326
00:25:02,475 --> 00:25:04,129
Huh?

327
00:27:54,516 --> 00:27:55,691
Aang!

328
00:28:23,502 --> 00:28:26,200
Team Avatar to the rescue!

329
00:28:27,506 --> 00:28:28,637
Aang!

330
00:28:29,334 --> 00:28:30,422
You made it!

331
00:28:31,075 --> 00:28:33,381
You couldn't wait a day
before running off to get yourself killed?

332
00:28:33,468 --> 00:28:35,949
I thought you were here
looking for a staff.

333
00:28:36,036 --> 00:28:37,342
Who's this guy?

334
00:28:43,957 --> 00:28:45,524
An Airbender.

335
00:29:06,545 --> 00:29:09,069
How did he hold up
an entire mountain?

336
00:29:09,156 --> 00:29:12,072
His chi is strong,
like nothing I've ever felt.

337
00:29:13,726 --> 00:29:16,207
Hey, Avatar, you think
this guy beat your record

338
00:29:16,294 --> 00:29:18,470
for longest frozen Airbender?

339
00:29:18,557 --> 00:29:21,516
Yeah. How long do you think
he was in that ice?

340
00:29:21,603 --> 00:29:22,735
I don't know.

341
00:29:23,257 --> 00:29:25,564
His tattoos look... ancient.

342
00:29:26,173 --> 00:29:28,088
He's been in there a long time.

343
00:29:28,175 --> 00:29:29,698
He smells good for an old guy.

344
00:29:29,785 --> 00:29:30,830
Ew.
What?

345
00:29:31,091 --> 00:29:32,701
My senses tell me this guy
is pretty attractive.

346
00:29:32,788 --> 00:29:34,051
Toph!Someone else confirm.

347
00:29:34,138 --> 00:29:35,966
This is serious.
What does attractive even mean?

348
00:29:36,053 --> 00:29:37,619
Just give me
a straight confirmation.

349
00:29:37,706 --> 00:29:38,794
Is he attractive?

350
00:29:38,969 --> 00:29:40,231
He's very attractive.
Huh?

351
00:29:41,580 --> 00:29:43,495
What? He is.

352
00:29:43,582 --> 00:29:44,931
It's all in the bone structure.

353
00:29:45,018 --> 00:29:46,324
No...

354
00:29:47,847 --> 00:29:48,892
No...

355
00:29:49,370 --> 00:29:50,371
No!

356
00:29:50,458 --> 00:29:52,069
Whoa, whoa, whoa. Hey.

357
00:29:52,156 --> 00:29:54,158
Easy, you're safe.

358
00:29:56,551 --> 00:29:58,075
-Earthbender!
-No, no, no!

359
00:29:58,162 --> 00:30:00,120
We're all friends here.
It's okay.

360
00:30:00,686 --> 00:30:02,079
Someone woke up
on the wrong side

361
00:30:02,166 --> 00:30:03,167
of the mountain.

362
00:30:04,037 --> 00:30:05,212
Where is she?

363
00:30:06,692 --> 00:30:08,520
Where is Avatar Sonam?

364
00:30:08,607 --> 00:30:09,913
You knew Sonam?

365
00:30:11,392 --> 00:30:12,698
Who are you?

366
00:30:13,351 --> 00:30:15,657
I don't know how to explain it,

367
00:30:15,744 --> 00:30:17,877
but you've been asleep
for a long time.

368
00:30:19,139 --> 00:30:20,532
I'm the Avatar now.

369
00:30:21,054 --> 00:30:22,055
I'm Aang.

370
00:30:23,230 --> 00:30:26,103
If you're the Avatar, then...

371
00:30:27,278 --> 00:30:28,279
Sonam...

372
00:30:30,803 --> 00:30:33,980
Well, Sonam might be long gone,

373
00:30:34,067 --> 00:30:37,157
but on the bright side,
you woke up at the perfect time.

374
00:30:37,244 --> 00:30:39,725
Everyone will be amazed
to see another Airbender.

375
00:30:39,812 --> 00:30:41,988
Aang's not the last one anymore.

376
00:30:43,511 --> 00:30:45,861
What do you mean, last?

377
00:30:49,996 --> 00:30:53,434
The Air Nomads,
they've been wiped out.

378
00:30:55,306 --> 00:30:56,437
There's only me.

379
00:30:58,352 --> 00:30:59,440
No.

380
00:31:00,398 --> 00:31:02,922
Sonam's staff,
do you have it?

381
00:31:03,662 --> 00:31:04,880
It's our only hope now.

382
00:31:05,751 --> 00:31:07,100
What do you mean?

383
00:31:07,187 --> 00:31:08,580
I thought it was a weapon.

384
00:31:09,842 --> 00:31:11,409
The staff is no weapon.

385
00:31:12,323 --> 00:31:13,541
It is a gift.

386
00:31:16,022 --> 00:31:18,851
<i>With it, </i>
<i>Sonam was able to channel</i>

387
00:31:18,938 --> 00:31:20,896
<i>the vast power</i>
<i>of the Spirit World.</i>

388
00:31:21,723 --> 00:31:25,031
<i>It was this power that </i>
<i>allowed Jharana to flourish.</i>

389
00:31:25,727 --> 00:31:30,167
<i>The greatest city in the world, </i>
<i>an Air Nomad utopia,</i>

390
00:31:30,254 --> 00:31:34,171
<i>where Sonam presided </i>
<i>over a golden age of balance</i>

391
00:31:34,258 --> 00:31:37,391
<i>and where I devoted my life </i>
<i>to serving her.</i>

392
00:31:38,131 --> 00:31:40,177
<i>In return, she raised me up</i>

393
00:31:40,264 --> 00:31:44,311
<i>and used her staff to give me, </i>
<i>a lowly Nonbender,</i>

394
00:31:44,398 --> 00:31:46,487
<i>the power to bend the air.</i>

395
00:31:47,793 --> 00:31:50,578
<i>I was the first, </i>
<i>but I would not be the last.</i>

396
00:31:51,666 --> 00:31:53,538
<i>She filled the skies</i>
<i>with Airbenders,</i>

397
00:31:54,495 --> 00:31:56,062
<i>and we flew by her side,</i>

398
00:31:56,149 --> 00:31:58,021
<i>spreading peace</i>
<i>across the world.</i>

399
00:32:07,030 --> 00:32:09,249
Aang? Are you okay?

400
00:32:10,946 --> 00:32:13,340
Sonam used the staff
to give people airbending.

401
00:32:14,385 --> 00:32:15,603
If we found it...

402
00:32:17,649 --> 00:32:20,391
I could bring airbending
back to the world!

403
00:32:20,478 --> 00:32:21,957
This is incredible!

404
00:32:22,045 --> 00:32:24,482
There haven't been Airbenders
for over a hundred years!

405
00:32:25,439 --> 00:32:28,181
This is everything
you ever wanted, Aang.

406
00:32:29,922 --> 00:32:32,055
We could heal
the greatest atrocity

407
00:32:32,142 --> 00:32:33,926
my nation committed
in the war.

408
00:32:34,927 --> 00:32:37,973
This could be the final step
to rebuilding the world.

409
00:32:38,061 --> 00:32:41,194
Not if the Denied
get there first. They have the map.

410
00:32:42,326 --> 00:32:43,631
Who are the Denied?

411
00:32:43,718 --> 00:32:45,807
A group of violent Nonbenders.

412
00:32:45,894 --> 00:32:47,113
They...

413
00:32:47,418 --> 00:32:50,334
They must be after the staff
to give themselves airbending.

414
00:32:50,421 --> 00:32:54,207
Then there's no time to waste.
There's only one place it could be.

415
00:32:54,294 --> 00:32:55,513
Ready your bison.

416
00:32:55,600 --> 00:32:57,993
We'll need to travel
across the endless ocean.

417
00:32:58,081 --> 00:33:01,214
On the other side of the world?
But there's nothing out there.

418
00:33:01,301 --> 00:33:02,911
There's an island.

419
00:33:02,998 --> 00:33:04,957
The journey will not be easy.

420
00:33:05,044 --> 00:33:06,306
But we can make it.

421
00:33:07,525 --> 00:33:09,004
Then let's get going.

422
00:33:10,441 --> 00:33:12,356
The skies are no place
for a water child.

423
00:33:13,008 --> 00:33:14,358
Water child?

424
00:33:15,010 --> 00:33:18,623
Um, I know you just woke up
after thousands of years,

425
00:33:18,710 --> 00:33:20,581
but we do
these things together.

426
00:33:20,668 --> 00:33:23,062
Trust me.
We're stronger this way.

427
00:33:23,149 --> 00:33:24,759
Welcome to Team Avatar.

428
00:33:25,369 --> 00:33:26,500
What's your name?

429
00:33:27,327 --> 00:33:28,633
Tagah.

430
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:30,156
My name is Tagah.

431
00:33:40,166 --> 00:33:42,908
Just think of it
as a big metal air bison.

432
00:33:51,046 --> 00:33:53,962
<i>We will travel </i>
<i>ancient paths through the sky.</i>

433
00:33:55,616 --> 00:33:57,096
<i>Ones that our people learned</i>

434
00:33:57,183 --> 00:33:59,229
<i>by following </i>
<i>the great air bison herds</i>

435
00:33:59,316 --> 00:34:01,361
<i>that long ago</i>
<i>taught us airbending.</i>

436
00:34:02,319 --> 00:34:03,929
<i>Air currents known only to us,</i>

437
00:34:04,930 --> 00:34:07,672
<i>encircling the great sphere </i>
<i>of existence,</i>

438
00:34:08,325 --> 00:34:10,631
<i>allowing us to travel</i>
<i>where we wish,</i>

439
00:34:11,415 --> 00:34:15,158
<i>giving us our name,</i>
<i>the Air Nomads.</i>

440
00:34:44,883 --> 00:34:46,493
What's he doing?

441
00:34:47,190 --> 00:34:48,974
He's really feeling that air.

442
00:34:49,061 --> 00:34:51,890
He's navigating by instinct.

443
00:34:51,977 --> 00:34:54,240
What if his instincts
are just wrong?

444
00:34:54,327 --> 00:34:56,808
Who needs instincts
when you've got muscles like that?

445
00:34:56,895 --> 00:34:59,506
Or what if
his brain is messed up from being frozen?

446
00:34:59,593 --> 00:35:02,509
Like me?
Uh, no, no!

447
00:35:02,596 --> 00:35:05,251
He was frozen for
five thousand years, okay?

448
00:35:05,338 --> 00:35:07,166
You were frozen for,
what, a hundred?

449
00:35:07,253 --> 00:35:09,429
Okay, that's nothing.
Your brain is...

450
00:35:10,517 --> 00:35:11,910
fresh.

451
00:35:11,997 --> 00:35:14,739
Maybe he is
a little old-fashioned, but look at him.

452
00:35:15,261 --> 00:35:16,871
He's so in tune
with his element,

453
00:35:16,958 --> 00:35:19,787
he can travel
across the entire ocean

454
00:35:19,874 --> 00:35:21,963
with no map,
no instruments.

455
00:35:24,139 --> 00:35:26,707
There's so much I can learn from him.

456
00:35:38,676 --> 00:35:41,722
I'd give anything to be able
to see my air bison again.

457
00:35:45,509 --> 00:35:49,208
And now,
to see only one remains.

458
00:35:51,428 --> 00:35:55,258
Aang, you said our people
were wiped out,

459
00:35:55,867 --> 00:35:57,129
yet you survived.

460
00:35:57,695 --> 00:35:58,739
How?

461
00:36:00,785 --> 00:36:03,091
I had just found out
I was the Avatar.

462
00:36:03,875 --> 00:36:07,531
But the responsibility,
it was too much.

463
00:36:09,489 --> 00:36:10,708
So I ran away.

464
00:36:12,144 --> 00:36:15,408
And while I was gone,
the Fire Nation attacked.

465
00:36:17,976 --> 00:36:19,325
They were looking for me.

466
00:36:21,284 --> 00:36:22,328
If...

467
00:36:23,329 --> 00:36:24,765
If I'd just been there.

468
00:36:25,331 --> 00:36:26,941
Sonam would say,

469
00:36:27,028 --> 00:36:29,683
Air Nomads are formed
from the mist.

470
00:36:30,380 --> 00:36:32,643
We walk the world
for a moment in time,

471
00:36:33,296 --> 00:36:36,429
then we return
to the eternal wind.

472
00:36:38,083 --> 00:36:39,650
Monk Gyatso taught me that.

473
00:36:40,781 --> 00:36:42,696
We carry the same weight,

474
00:36:42,783 --> 00:36:45,786
a grief no one else
could possibly comprehend.

475
00:36:45,873 --> 00:36:48,659
But you and I
can heal the past.

476
00:36:49,312 --> 00:36:52,750
Let me show you how powerful
our element can be

477
00:36:52,837 --> 00:36:54,752
when Airbenders work together.

478
00:36:58,146 --> 00:36:59,887
Tagah, what are you doing?

479
00:36:59,974 --> 00:37:01,280
Whoa!

480
00:37:01,367 --> 00:37:03,195
This is how Sonam taught me.

481
00:37:03,282 --> 00:37:05,502
Feel the energy that tethers us.

482
00:37:11,595 --> 00:37:14,337
The bond between us.
Can you feel it?

483
00:37:14,424 --> 00:37:15,512
Use it!

484
00:37:15,599 --> 00:37:16,904
This is amazing!

485
00:37:18,079 --> 00:37:19,559
Yeah!

486
00:37:22,257 --> 00:37:23,824
Woo-hoo!

487
00:37:23,911 --> 00:37:26,218
Oh, yeah!
Human boomerang!

488
00:37:26,305 --> 00:37:27,524
He's actually flying.

489
00:37:27,611 --> 00:37:28,960
So are we.

490
00:37:29,047 --> 00:37:31,179
Whoa, that's my best friend!
That's my best friend!

491
00:37:32,572 --> 00:37:33,834
Now you throw me!

492
00:38:02,602 --> 00:38:04,735
I had no idea
this was possible!

493
00:38:04,822 --> 00:38:06,563
This is only the beginning.

494
00:38:14,135 --> 00:38:15,702
I can't believe it.

495
00:38:16,355 --> 00:38:18,183
Airbenders will fill
the sky again.

496
00:38:18,705 --> 00:38:20,707
We have been
given a great gift.

497
00:38:21,316 --> 00:38:23,101
The chance to redeem ourselves.

498
00:38:24,015 --> 00:38:26,670
You were destined to find me
on that mountain, Aang.

499
00:38:28,759 --> 00:38:30,456
How did you end up there?

500
00:38:34,417 --> 00:38:36,549
The Earthbenders
had attacked Jharana.

501
00:38:37,332 --> 00:38:39,813
Sonam and I fought fearlessly,
side by side.

502
00:38:40,466 --> 00:38:42,773
We drove them
back to Mount Baihu,

503
00:38:42,860 --> 00:38:44,731
and that's the last
I remember.

504
00:38:46,690 --> 00:38:48,343
She must have saved your life.

505
00:38:48,909 --> 00:38:51,346
Only an Avatar could have
put you in that sphere.

506
00:38:55,176 --> 00:38:58,223
Aang, can I ask you something?

507
00:38:58,310 --> 00:38:59,354
Of course.

508
00:38:59,877 --> 00:39:02,575
If the Fire Nation
destroyed the Air Nomads...

509
00:39:03,620 --> 00:39:06,318
how can you suffer
the presence of the Fire Lord?

510
00:39:09,408 --> 00:39:11,366
Zuko is a friend and an ally.

511
00:39:12,019 --> 00:39:14,892
He turned against
his own father to help me end the war.

512
00:39:14,979 --> 00:39:17,547
Yet he wears
the crown himself now.

513
00:39:18,765 --> 00:39:21,420
Fire by its nature burns, Aang.

514
00:39:22,421 --> 00:39:25,816
Our kind have always
suffered at the hands of the other elements.

515
00:39:27,382 --> 00:39:29,167
That's why
we built Republic City.

516
00:39:29,863 --> 00:39:32,300
To show the world that
if we listen to each other,

517
00:39:32,387 --> 00:39:34,520
we can all live
together in peace.

518
00:39:36,348 --> 00:39:38,219
And once
we bring back Airbenders,

519
00:39:39,046 --> 00:39:40,395
it'll be complete.

520
00:39:43,790 --> 00:39:45,966
When everyone stuck
to their own,

521
00:39:46,053 --> 00:39:48,186
the whole world
was nearly torn apart.

522
00:39:49,187 --> 00:39:53,539
And besides, Katara,
Sokka, Zuko, Toph...

523
00:39:53,626 --> 00:39:55,106
they're my family now.

524
00:39:56,629 --> 00:39:59,327
I want to live in a world
where we can all be together.

525
00:40:00,938 --> 00:40:03,201
You remind me so much of Sonam.

526
00:40:08,032 --> 00:40:09,424
It's the Avatar.

527
00:40:09,512 --> 00:40:11,862
And this time he's got
his friends with him.

528
00:40:11,949 --> 00:40:13,690
That's the Fire Lord's airship!

529
00:40:13,777 --> 00:40:16,127
How'd they get ahead of us?
They don't even have the map!

530
00:40:16,736 --> 00:40:18,608
We can't risk him
getting to the staff first.

531
00:40:18,695 --> 00:40:19,652
Kill him.

532
00:40:19,739 --> 00:40:21,045
But he spared our lives.

533
00:40:22,002 --> 00:40:24,178
And how many countless were
killed in the hundred years

534
00:40:24,265 --> 00:40:25,484
waiting for his return?

535
00:40:25,571 --> 00:40:28,139
Where was he when
your family was wiped out?

536
00:40:28,226 --> 00:40:29,749
If we want anything to change,

537
00:40:29,836 --> 00:40:32,796
we need what
the Benders have... Power.

538
00:40:40,978 --> 00:40:42,109
Fire!

539
00:40:47,854 --> 00:40:49,203
It's the Denied!

540
00:40:52,032 --> 00:40:53,947
Uh, we are definitely
under attack!

541
00:40:55,732 --> 00:40:57,124
Tear them to shreds!

542
00:41:10,224 --> 00:41:11,878
Is he crushing the ship?

543
00:41:14,098 --> 00:41:15,055
Tagah?

544
00:41:16,013 --> 00:41:17,231
Tagah, stop!

545
00:41:42,517 --> 00:41:43,606
We're here.

546
00:41:45,738 --> 00:41:47,479
The Immortal Storm.

547
00:41:48,088 --> 00:41:49,133
Oh, no.

548
00:41:54,704 --> 00:41:57,358
There has to be
another way around. No!

549
00:41:57,445 --> 00:41:59,752
Together, you and I
can clear a path for the ship.

550
00:41:59,839 --> 00:42:01,014
But we have to go now.

551
00:42:02,059 --> 00:42:04,278
Aang, trust me.

552
00:42:07,673 --> 00:42:09,762
Uh, maybe now's
a good time to turn back.

553
00:42:09,849 --> 00:42:12,243
I don't think
that's an option anymore.

554
00:42:12,330 --> 00:42:13,461
Where are they going?

555
00:42:22,340 --> 00:42:24,429
The engine's out.
We're losing air pressure.

556
00:42:26,387 --> 00:42:27,519
Whoa!

557
00:42:30,304 --> 00:42:32,611
Katara, Toph, come with me.
What about me?

558
00:42:32,698 --> 00:42:33,743
Take the wheel.

559
00:42:34,178 --> 00:42:36,484
What? No, I've only ever
crashed Fire Nation airships.

560
00:42:38,225 --> 00:42:39,879
Okay, let's see.
Here's our rudder,

561
00:42:39,966 --> 00:42:41,576
this is the elevator,
there's our ballast,

562
00:42:41,664 --> 00:42:43,840
and there's the giant tornado
that's going to kill us all.

563
00:42:47,582 --> 00:42:48,888
Follow my lead.

564
00:43:00,204 --> 00:43:02,467
Work with me,
just like I showed you.

565
00:43:03,381 --> 00:43:04,948
We can harness the air.

566
00:43:15,262 --> 00:43:17,438
Yes! That's it, Aang! Keep going!

567
00:43:27,884 --> 00:43:29,886
There's a long tear
above your head on the left.

568
00:43:29,973 --> 00:43:31,017
Got it!

569
00:43:31,496 --> 00:43:34,194
Whatever happens,
you have to hold the ship together.

570
00:43:34,281 --> 00:43:36,066
<i>Zuko! Zuko!</i>

571
00:43:36,153 --> 00:43:38,155
Aang and Tagah
are destroying tornadoes,

572
00:43:38,242 --> 00:43:40,853
but there's too many,
and they're everywhere!

573
00:43:40,940 --> 00:43:43,029
Just steer the ship.
Don't lose Aang.

574
00:43:43,116 --> 00:43:44,291
It's not that easy,

575
00:43:44,422 --> 00:43:46,641
especially when
everything is sideways.

576
00:43:46,729 --> 00:43:48,382
Okay, left!

577
00:43:56,564 --> 00:43:58,741
I did it!

578
00:43:58,828 --> 00:44:00,612
Right!

579
00:44:08,881 --> 00:44:10,796
Oh, no!
We're falling behind!

580
00:44:12,058 --> 00:44:14,669
I'm losing sight of them!
We have to go back!

581
00:44:14,757 --> 00:44:16,149
Trust in your friends.

582
00:44:16,236 --> 00:44:18,499
They won't make it
if we don't clear a path.

583
00:44:31,774 --> 00:44:34,167
Zuko! We're gonna
crash into the sea!

584
00:44:34,254 --> 00:44:37,257
When I give you the signal,
pull the lever next to the wheel.

585
00:44:41,522 --> 00:44:43,089
We're gonna crash! We're gonna crash!

586
00:44:43,873 --> 00:44:44,874
Katara?

587
00:45:04,807 --> 00:45:06,330
Give me the signal!
Give me the signal!

588
00:45:11,204 --> 00:45:12,249
It's closed!

589
00:45:13,859 --> 00:45:15,252
Sokka, now!

590
00:45:15,339 --> 00:45:16,644
Here we go!

591
00:45:39,406 --> 00:45:41,408
Katara! We did it!

592
00:45:42,496 --> 00:45:43,933
What were you thinking?

593
00:45:44,020 --> 00:45:45,760
I was clearing the tornadoes
to make a path.

594
00:45:45,848 --> 00:45:48,111
The ship almost crashed, Aang.
We could have died.

595
00:45:48,198 --> 00:45:50,287
And what if you got yourself killed?

596
00:45:50,374 --> 00:45:51,375
You're the Avatar.

597
00:45:51,549 --> 00:45:54,247
This is too risky.
We need to turn back now.

598
00:45:54,334 --> 00:45:56,728
No! We're almost there.

599
00:45:56,815 --> 00:45:59,557
We just need to get
to the eye of the storm.

600
00:46:00,253 --> 00:46:02,821
Aang, no.
This is too dangerous.

601
00:46:02,908 --> 00:46:05,650
The staff is out there.
The Denied are after it.

602
00:46:05,737 --> 00:46:08,174
Do you really believe
that they could make it through the storm?

603
00:46:08,261 --> 00:46:09,523
We're nearly there.

604
00:46:09,610 --> 00:46:11,569
That staff
can bring back my people.

605
00:46:11,656 --> 00:46:13,005
I understand how much
you want that, but...

606
00:46:13,092 --> 00:46:15,051
You don't understand.
None of you do.

607
00:46:16,400 --> 00:46:17,705
Aang...

608
00:46:19,751 --> 00:46:20,839
We push forward.

609
00:46:24,799 --> 00:46:27,585
If we generate enough air, we can push our way through.

610
00:47:11,716 --> 00:47:13,761
We're alive?

611
00:47:14,545 --> 00:47:17,156
We made it through.
Thank you, Tagah.

612
00:47:17,243 --> 00:47:19,985
It was you, Aang.
We're here because of you.

613
00:47:20,072 --> 00:47:21,856
Yeah, we're having
a good time, too.

614
00:47:21,944 --> 00:47:24,337
You could have told us
we were flying into the Immortal Storm.

615
00:47:24,424 --> 00:47:26,949
I know it was dangerous,
but we had to risk it.

616
00:47:27,036 --> 00:47:28,211
We?

617
00:47:28,298 --> 00:47:30,430
I don't remember when
we took a vote on that.

618
00:47:30,517 --> 00:47:32,650
There wasn't time.
I had to make a call.

619
00:47:32,737 --> 00:47:34,652
Friends, please,
don't blame Aang.

620
00:47:34,739 --> 00:47:36,306
This is all my fault.

621
00:47:36,393 --> 00:47:38,003
I knew this would be difficult.

622
00:47:39,048 --> 00:47:41,615
But Aang believed
in your strength as a team.

623
00:47:41,702 --> 00:47:43,530
And I'm honored
to be a part of it.

624
00:47:49,710 --> 00:47:51,190
I forgive you, Tagah.

625
00:47:51,756 --> 00:47:53,323
Everyone, look.

626
00:47:54,889 --> 00:47:58,893
These islands,
they were Lion Turtles.

627
00:48:00,895 --> 00:48:01,853
Whoa.

628
00:48:03,376 --> 00:48:04,856
It's beautiful.

629
00:48:07,163 --> 00:48:08,947
Long before my time,

630
00:48:09,034 --> 00:48:10,818
the Lion Turtles
granted the gift

631
00:48:10,905 --> 00:48:12,472
of bending to humans.

632
00:48:13,212 --> 00:48:16,128
These are their final
resting grounds.

633
00:48:16,215 --> 00:48:19,262
This is where Sonam came
to learn their ways.

634
00:48:20,176 --> 00:48:23,570
I am certain that
she left her staff here.

635
00:48:23,788 --> 00:48:25,398
Where should we start looking?

636
00:48:25,485 --> 00:48:28,184
Aang, you must
connect with her.

637
00:48:29,011 --> 00:48:31,970
But no one
can connect with Sonam.

638
00:48:32,057 --> 00:48:34,016
The spiritual power
of the Lion Turtles

639
00:48:34,103 --> 00:48:35,800
is still
concentrated here.

640
00:48:35,887 --> 00:48:37,323
Let it guide you.

641
00:48:37,932 --> 00:48:39,412
We'll set out immediately.

642
00:48:39,499 --> 00:48:42,502
Actually, Tagah,
we could really use your help here.

643
00:48:42,589 --> 00:48:45,723
If the Denied are close behind,
we need to be ready.

644
00:48:45,810 --> 00:48:48,378
Yeah, and we're gonna need more
than Toph's metal bending

645
00:48:48,465 --> 00:48:49,553
to fix this ship.

646
00:48:49,640 --> 00:48:51,555
My bending got us
through that storm.

647
00:48:51,642 --> 00:48:52,773
What did you do?

648
00:48:52,860 --> 00:48:54,036
Steered with his feet.

649
00:48:54,123 --> 00:48:55,472
Repairs can wait.

650
00:48:55,559 --> 00:48:56,864
Aang needs me.

651
00:48:56,951 --> 00:49:00,390
Tagah, please,
stay and help my friends.

652
00:49:01,217 --> 00:49:02,740
I'll be okay on my own.

653
00:49:03,436 --> 00:49:04,698
As you wish.

654
00:49:05,177 --> 00:49:07,701
We will begin repairs
for our voyage home.

655
00:49:09,747 --> 00:49:13,664
Everyone, I know
I've asked a lot of you on this journey,

656
00:49:13,751 --> 00:49:15,927
but we're about
to accomplish something

657
00:49:16,014 --> 00:49:17,711
that will change the world.

658
00:50:09,285 --> 00:50:10,808
Let it guide you.

659
00:50:27,129 --> 00:50:28,434
Sonam?

660
00:50:46,757 --> 00:50:50,587
Oh, this is turning out to be
a nice little vacation.

661
00:50:50,674 --> 00:50:52,937
Aside from all the people
trying to kill us.

662
00:50:53,024 --> 00:50:54,068
And the tornadoes.

663
00:50:54,156 --> 00:50:56,636
Um, we're supposed
to be fixing the ship?

664
00:50:56,723 --> 00:50:58,508
You're doing great, buddy.

665
00:50:58,595 --> 00:51:00,684
Has anyone seen Tagah?

666
00:51:00,771 --> 00:51:02,555
Yes, we've all seen Tagah.

667
00:51:02,642 --> 00:51:04,905
He's so gorgeous.
Jeez, I get it.

668
00:51:05,689 --> 00:51:06,951
Oh, I see what you mean.

669
00:51:07,038 --> 00:51:08,735
He wandered off that way.

670
00:51:08,822 --> 00:51:10,955
No, maybe that way?

671
00:51:44,815 --> 00:51:45,990
Tagah!

672
00:51:46,599 --> 00:51:47,557
Where are you going?

673
00:51:48,645 --> 00:51:50,124
Aang needs to be protected.

674
00:51:50,777 --> 00:51:51,865
I agree.

675
00:51:54,694 --> 00:51:57,523
I know my ways
may seem unusual to you,

676
00:51:57,610 --> 00:52:00,526
but I assure you,
everything I do,

677
00:52:00,613 --> 00:52:02,006
I do for Aang.

678
00:52:02,093 --> 00:52:04,530
For Aang?
Or for the staff?

679
00:52:06,053 --> 00:52:08,752
You have no idea
all that we've lost.

680
00:52:08,839 --> 00:52:11,015
You've never known
a world with Airbenders.

681
00:52:11,798 --> 00:52:13,278
I know Aang.

682
00:52:14,105 --> 00:52:16,194
<i>He may be the last of his kind,</i>

683
00:52:16,281 --> 00:52:18,544
<i>but he's the reason</i>
<i>this world knows peace.</i>

684
00:52:22,548 --> 00:52:26,030
<i>His values as an Air Nomad </i>
<i>have brought balance to chaos.</i>

685
00:52:28,685 --> 00:52:31,992
<i>It's because of Aang</i>
<i>that the Water Tribes,</i>

686
00:52:32,079 --> 00:52:35,474
<i>Earth Kingdom, and Fire Nation </i>
<i>now work together,</i>

687
00:52:35,561 --> 00:52:37,694
<i>striving for harmony,</i>

688
00:52:37,781 --> 00:52:40,044
<i>a peace we once</i>
<i>thought unattainable.</i>

689
00:52:42,786 --> 00:52:44,527
<i>You speak of peace.</i>

690
00:52:44,614 --> 00:52:47,573
There will never be peace
among the elements.

691
00:52:47,660 --> 00:52:48,792
<i>There never was.</i>

692
00:52:48,966 --> 00:52:52,143
<i>Your precious Republic City </i>
<i>is built on lies.</i>

693
00:52:52,230 --> 00:52:54,406
<i>It's built on hope.</i>

694
00:52:54,493 --> 00:52:56,016
<i>Do you have hope, Tagah?</i>

695
00:52:56,103 --> 00:52:59,063
Saving my people requires
more than just hope.

696
00:52:59,150 --> 00:53:01,021
It requires sacrifice.

697
00:53:01,108 --> 00:53:04,068
I saw you try to crush
the Denied's airships.

698
00:53:04,155 --> 00:53:05,591
You were ready to kill them.

699
00:53:08,115 --> 00:53:10,596
<i>I know what kind</i>
<i>of Airbender Aang is...</i>

700
00:53:13,338 --> 00:53:15,297
but what kind
of Airbender are you?

701
00:53:44,238 --> 00:53:45,979
Aang did well
getting us here.

702
00:53:46,545 --> 00:53:50,114
There is great strength in him,
but weakness as well.

703
00:53:50,201 --> 00:53:51,420
Weakness?

704
00:53:51,507 --> 00:53:52,725
Yes.

705
00:53:52,812 --> 00:53:53,944
You.

706
00:54:10,482 --> 00:54:11,614
What the hog monkey?

707
00:54:15,531 --> 00:54:16,401
No!

708
00:54:35,289 --> 00:54:36,813
He trusted you!

709
00:54:43,863 --> 00:54:44,908
No.

710
00:54:48,651 --> 00:54:50,000
You traitor!

711
00:55:38,091 --> 00:55:39,310
Tagah!

712
00:56:05,336 --> 00:56:06,337
Brother.

713
00:56:09,383 --> 00:56:11,560
Tagah. It's real.

714
00:56:16,216 --> 00:56:18,392
We can finally
bring back airbending.

715
00:56:21,744 --> 00:56:22,962
Let's go tell the others.

716
00:56:23,049 --> 00:56:24,442
We can do this.

717
00:56:25,008 --> 00:56:26,313
Me and you.

718
00:56:27,097 --> 00:56:28,881
I can't do this
without my friends.

719
00:56:31,275 --> 00:56:34,496
Earth killed my people.
Fire killed yours.

720
00:56:34,583 --> 00:56:38,456
The staff is the only way
we can create a new Air Empire.

721
00:56:38,543 --> 00:56:40,806
One capable of defending itself.

722
00:56:40,893 --> 00:56:42,112
No.

723
00:56:42,199 --> 00:56:44,244
We can build
a new future, Tagah.

724
00:56:44,331 --> 00:56:46,420
But it has to be for everyone.

725
00:56:46,508 --> 00:56:48,553
The staff doesn't
belong to everyone.

726
00:56:48,640 --> 00:56:49,946
It belongs to us.

727
00:56:50,033 --> 00:56:51,991
What...
What have you done?

728
00:56:52,122 --> 00:56:55,778
As long as they were
around, you'd always put them ahead of our people.

729
00:56:55,865 --> 00:56:59,216
Don't you see?
This is how we redeem ourselves.

730
00:56:59,999 --> 00:57:01,740
It doesn't matter
that you ran then.

731
00:57:01,827 --> 00:57:03,960
As long as you stand
with me now.

732
00:57:04,047 --> 00:57:06,789
No... Katara.
Aang, listen to me.

733
00:57:06,876 --> 00:57:08,181
This is the only way.

734
00:57:22,152 --> 00:57:23,980
You're a traitor to your own.

735
00:57:24,067 --> 00:57:26,069
Just like Sonam.

736
00:58:04,063 --> 00:58:06,370
I wanted to do this
with you by my side.

737
00:58:07,632 --> 00:58:09,939
But if I must build
the new Air Empire alone...

738
00:58:11,114 --> 00:58:12,332
so be it.

739
00:58:20,819 --> 00:58:23,953
There's no way in!
We have to turn back!

740
00:58:24,040 --> 00:58:26,738
No! We keep trying
to push through!

741
00:58:39,316 --> 00:58:40,839
Sonam's staff.

742
00:58:41,927 --> 00:58:43,320
Denied...

743
00:58:43,407 --> 00:58:45,191
the Avatar is dead.

744
00:58:45,714 --> 00:58:48,368
If you wish to build a new world
where you have the power,

745
00:58:48,455 --> 00:58:50,066
I can give it to you.

746
00:59:05,429 --> 00:59:06,691
Appa!

747
00:59:06,778 --> 00:59:07,866
Katara!

748
00:59:08,606 --> 00:59:09,825
Katara!

749
00:59:11,304 --> 00:59:12,392
Katara.

750
00:59:13,176 --> 00:59:14,438
They're gone.

751
00:59:15,178 --> 00:59:16,483
It's all my fault.

752
00:59:17,571 --> 00:59:19,095
It's always been my fault.

753
00:59:19,704 --> 00:59:21,488
Ever since I ran away.

754
00:59:23,447 --> 00:59:26,885
No Avatar has ever
fallen into such shame

755
00:59:26,972 --> 00:59:28,931
as to join me
here in my sorrow.

756
00:59:31,150 --> 00:59:32,891
Why do you grieve so, friend?

757
00:59:33,500 --> 00:59:35,415
Avatar Sonam?

758
00:59:38,288 --> 00:59:39,855
Tagah murdered my friends.

759
00:59:40,638 --> 00:59:42,292
And now he has the staff.

760
00:59:42,379 --> 00:59:44,250
Tagah? No.

761
00:59:44,337 --> 00:59:46,688
No, I... I stopped him.

762
00:59:47,210 --> 00:59:48,559
I hid the staff.

763
00:59:49,125 --> 00:59:51,214
What have you done?

764
00:59:52,128 --> 00:59:54,217
You're the one
who gave him airbending!

765
00:59:54,739 --> 00:59:57,046
How could you give power
to a monster?

766
00:59:57,699 --> 01:00:01,137
The Tagah I gave bending to
was a different man.

767
01:00:02,878 --> 01:00:04,444
<i>It was a different time.</i>

768
01:00:05,358 --> 01:00:08,187
<i>The Airbenders were</i>
<i>the peacekeepers</i> <i>of the four elements.</i>

769
01:00:08,840 --> 01:00:11,321
<i>We used our power</i>
<i>to mediate all conflict</i>

770
01:00:11,408 --> 01:00:12,626
<i>with non-violence.</i>

771
01:00:13,279 --> 01:00:15,107
<i>But we were</i>
<i>the fewest in numbers.</i>

772
01:00:16,282 --> 01:00:19,721
<i>For many years, we existed </i>
<i>in a beautiful balance</i>

773
01:00:19,808 --> 01:00:21,461
<i>of great prosperity.</i>

774
01:00:21,548 --> 01:00:23,333
<i>But the world began to shift.</i>

775
01:00:24,203 --> 01:00:26,597
<i>The Earthbenders </i>
<i>formed their own kingdom,</i>

776
01:00:26,684 --> 01:00:28,991
<i>separating from </i>
<i>the other elemental tribes.</i>

777
01:00:29,905 --> 01:00:31,776
<i>The balance of the world</i>
<i>was at risk.</i>

778
01:00:32,342 --> 01:00:34,344
<i>It was my duty to act.</i>

779
01:00:35,606 --> 01:00:37,390
<i>So I learned how</i>
<i>to channel the energy</i>

780
01:00:37,477 --> 01:00:39,871
<i>of the Spirit World </i>
<i>just as the Lion Turtles did.</i>

781
01:00:40,306 --> 01:00:43,048
<i>To give people </i>
<i>the power of airbending.</i>

782
01:00:44,180 --> 01:00:45,964
<i>My most devout pupil,</i>

783
01:00:46,051 --> 01:00:48,488
<i>Tagah, was the first</i>
<i>to receive it.</i>

784
01:00:49,620 --> 01:00:51,709
<i>I sent my new peacekeepers out</i>

785
01:00:51,796 --> 01:00:53,711
<i>to help calm</i>
<i>the growing unrest.</i>

786
01:00:54,756 --> 01:00:57,367
<i>But they were not prepared </i>
<i>for the brutality</i>

787
01:00:57,454 --> 01:00:59,282
<i>of the new Earth Kingdom.</i>

788
01:01:01,327 --> 01:01:02,807
<i>Tagah watched</i>

789
01:01:02,894 --> 01:01:06,028
<i>as his brothers and sisters </i>
<i>were all slaughtered.</i>

790
01:01:07,551 --> 01:01:10,293
<i>His heart darkened</i>
<i>by the violence of war.</i>

791
01:01:10,859 --> 01:01:14,776
<i>He now saw everyone</i>
<i>who wasn't an Air Nomad</i> <i>as the enemy.</i>

792
01:01:16,429 --> 01:01:18,736
<i>Tagah begged me to use </i>
<i>the staff to create an army</i>

793
01:01:18,823 --> 01:01:21,130
<i>and to kill </i>
<i>all who would do us harm.</i>

794
01:01:21,783 --> 01:01:23,132
<i>I refused.</i>

795
01:01:23,654 --> 01:01:24,742
<i>So he stole it.</i>

796
01:01:26,309 --> 01:01:28,398
<i>When he connected the staff </i> <i>to the temple,</i>

797
01:01:28,485 --> 01:01:31,618
<i>his energy was so corrupted </i>
<i>by grief and rage</i>

798
01:01:31,705 --> 01:01:33,316
<i>that the power</i>
<i>of the Spirit World</i>

799
01:01:33,403 --> 01:01:34,404
<i>consumed him.</i>

800
01:01:35,405 --> 01:01:38,495
<i>Tagah became something</i>
<i>more than human,</i>

801
01:01:38,582 --> 01:01:39,975
<i>too powerful to kill.</i>

802
01:01:41,367 --> 01:01:44,022
<i>It took all my energy</i>
<i>to finally trap him</i>

803
01:01:44,109 --> 01:01:47,460
<i>high above the clouds, </i>
<i>where no one would find him.</i>

804
01:01:48,548 --> 01:01:50,333
<i>I reclaimed the staff,</i>

805
01:01:50,942 --> 01:01:52,596
<i>but I was fatally wounded.</i>

806
01:01:53,379 --> 01:01:55,904
<i>Before the Earth Kingdom</i>
<i>could invade Jharana,</i>

807
01:01:55,991 --> 01:01:58,645
<i>I sent the remaining Air Nomads </i>
<i>into the mountains.</i>

808
01:01:59,777 --> 01:02:01,910
<i>And I hid my temple</i>
<i>in the Spirit World,</i>

809
01:02:01,997 --> 01:02:04,129
<i>where no one</i>
<i>could access its power.</i>

810
01:02:06,001 --> 01:02:08,438
<i>Then I locked the staff away,</i>

811
01:02:08,525 --> 01:02:10,744
<i>where only the Avatar</i>
<i>could find it.</i>

812
01:02:12,268 --> 01:02:15,140
<i>I died, hoping that one day,</i>

813
01:02:15,227 --> 01:02:17,751
<i>another Avatar would</i>
<i>create more Airbenders</i>

814
01:02:17,839 --> 01:02:19,884
<i>and restore balance</i>
<i>to this world.</i>

815
01:02:20,798 --> 01:02:23,453
And that Avatar is you, Aang.

816
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:25,107
You have to get my staff

817
01:02:25,194 --> 01:02:26,848
before Tagah connects it
to the temple.

818
01:02:27,544 --> 01:02:29,111
There's still time.

819
01:02:29,198 --> 01:02:31,156
Don't let my regret
become yours.

820
01:02:32,027 --> 01:02:34,290
My friends and I
fought hard for this peace.

821
01:02:34,812 --> 01:02:37,206
I won't let him
start another war.

822
01:02:37,293 --> 01:02:39,034
Help me find a way back.

823
01:02:40,600 --> 01:02:41,819
Sonam?

824
01:02:42,994 --> 01:02:44,213
What's happening?

825
01:02:46,302 --> 01:02:47,390
No!

826
01:02:47,477 --> 01:02:49,218
No! Please!

827
01:02:49,305 --> 01:02:50,654
I have to fix this!

828
01:02:50,741 --> 01:02:52,917
This can't be it!
I can't die yet!

829
01:02:53,004 --> 01:02:54,614
Please! Not yet!

830
01:02:54,701 --> 01:02:56,225
No!
<i>Aang?</i>

831
01:02:56,312 --> 01:02:58,053
Katara?
<i>I'm losing him.</i>

832
01:02:58,140 --> 01:03:00,533
<i>Come on, Aang!</i>
<i>Come on! Aang!</i>

833
01:03:00,620 --> 01:03:02,144
Hold on!

834
01:03:02,231 --> 01:03:03,493
Aang!

835
01:03:04,798 --> 01:03:05,887
Katara!

836
01:03:05,974 --> 01:03:07,192
I was so worried.

837
01:03:07,714 --> 01:03:08,802
Aang!

838
01:03:08,890 --> 01:03:10,848
Sokka!

839
01:03:10,935 --> 01:03:12,284
I knew you'd
pull through, buddy.

840
01:03:12,371 --> 01:03:13,285
Hey, Aang.

841
01:03:13,372 --> 01:03:14,460
Zuko!

842
01:03:14,547 --> 01:03:15,940
Momo!

843
01:03:16,593 --> 01:03:18,290
Welcome back, twinkle toes.

844
01:03:18,377 --> 01:03:20,162
Toph, you're okay.

845
01:03:20,249 --> 01:03:21,641
I...

846
01:03:21,728 --> 01:03:22,991
I thought you were all dead.

847
01:03:23,078 --> 01:03:26,385
We were.
But Katara saved us.

848
01:03:26,472 --> 01:03:28,387
<i>The spiritual power</i>
<i>of these waters</i>

849
01:03:28,474 --> 01:03:30,389
<i>strengthened</i>
<i>my healing abilities.</i>

850
01:03:33,305 --> 01:03:34,872
You're incredible, Katara.

851
01:03:36,874 --> 01:03:38,093
Where's Appa?

852
01:03:39,485 --> 01:03:40,922
Tagah must have taken him.

853
01:03:41,748 --> 01:03:42,836
I'm sorry.

854
01:03:43,359 --> 01:03:44,447
No.

855
01:03:45,752 --> 01:03:47,667
I can't believe I trusted him.

856
01:03:49,800 --> 01:03:51,410
We'll get through this.

857
01:03:54,065 --> 01:03:55,980
So, let me get this straight.

858
01:03:56,067 --> 01:03:59,027
He's pulling Sonam's temple
out of the Spirit World

859
01:03:59,114 --> 01:04:01,507
to gain unlimited power,
and let me guess,

860
01:04:01,594 --> 01:04:03,031
you want us to stop him?

861
01:04:04,162 --> 01:04:06,643
Sure, only problem
is your air bro

862
01:04:06,730 --> 01:04:09,254
crushed our ship
and stole your bison.

863
01:04:09,341 --> 01:04:12,344
Also, there's a massive
typhoon surrounding us!

864
01:04:15,478 --> 01:04:19,047
I don't say this very often,
but Sokka's right.

865
01:04:19,134 --> 01:04:21,310
Thank you.
Yep, we're stuck.

866
01:04:21,397 --> 01:04:22,833
And there aren't
enough Lion Turtles

867
01:04:22,920 --> 01:04:24,617
for all of us
to have our own island,

868
01:04:24,704 --> 01:04:26,315
so I'm calling this one.

869
01:04:26,402 --> 01:04:27,664
I'm naming him Snappy.

870
01:04:27,751 --> 01:04:29,971
Aw,
Snappy is the best one.

871
01:04:30,058 --> 01:04:31,233
I know.

872
01:04:31,320 --> 01:04:33,191
We may not know where Tagah is,

873
01:04:33,844 --> 01:04:35,280
but we know
what he's looking for

874
01:04:35,367 --> 01:04:36,716
is in the Spirit World.

875
01:04:37,413 --> 01:04:38,892
<i>And lucky for us,</i>

876
01:04:38,980 --> 01:04:41,112
<i>we're stuck in the most </i>
<i>spiritually charged place</i>

877
01:04:41,199 --> 01:04:42,287
<i>on the planet.</i>

878
01:04:42,984 --> 01:04:45,682
<i>So I may be able to open </i>
<i>a portal to get us there,</i>

879
01:04:45,769 --> 01:04:48,511
<i>if I can summon an old friend.</i>

880
01:04:57,041 --> 01:04:57,999
Wow.

881
01:04:59,087 --> 01:05:00,653
The ocean spirit.

882
01:05:08,879 --> 01:05:11,534
This portal smells an awful lot
like the fish market.

883
01:05:11,621 --> 01:05:13,405
I'm gonna go check on Snappy.

884
01:05:13,492 --> 01:05:15,146
Face your death with honor.

885
01:05:15,233 --> 01:05:16,539
I'm sorry.

886
01:05:16,626 --> 01:05:17,931
I know I got us into this,

887
01:05:18,019 --> 01:05:20,238
but I promise you
I'll fix it.

888
01:05:20,804 --> 01:05:22,110
We'll fix it...

889
01:05:22,675 --> 01:05:23,894
together.

890
01:05:27,115 --> 01:05:29,334
We're gonna die! We're gonna die!

891
01:05:29,421 --> 01:05:31,989
Woah!

892
01:05:40,084 --> 01:05:42,043
What?
Where's my power pony?

893
01:05:42,130 --> 01:05:44,828
Uh, were my hands
always this small?

894
01:05:44,915 --> 01:05:46,438
It's Baby Toph!

895
01:05:46,525 --> 01:05:49,224
Baby Toph!

896
01:05:49,311 --> 01:05:51,356
What the hog monkey?

897
01:05:51,443 --> 01:05:52,531
Old people!

898
01:05:52,618 --> 01:05:53,619
Gran Gran?

899
01:05:53,706 --> 01:05:55,665
It's your sister,
you meathead!

900
01:05:55,752 --> 01:05:58,059
Give me Toph.
There, there, Toph.

901
01:05:58,146 --> 01:05:59,930
Oh, no, Zuko!

902
01:06:00,017 --> 01:06:01,714
What happened
to your beautiful face?

903
01:06:01,801 --> 01:06:04,587
You look like a dried sea squid.

904
01:06:04,674 --> 01:06:06,067
No, Zuko!
Tired.

905
01:06:06,154 --> 01:06:08,156
Ow, ow, ow!
What's going on here?

906
01:06:08,939 --> 01:06:10,984
The Spirit World
is out of balance.

907
01:06:11,811 --> 01:06:13,248
And so are we.

908
01:06:15,467 --> 01:06:17,078
That's gotta be Tagah.

909
01:06:38,751 --> 01:06:40,275
Oh, no!

910
01:06:40,362 --> 01:06:42,668
He's pulling Sonam's temple
into our world!

911
01:06:42,755 --> 01:06:44,148
We're running out of time!

912
01:06:44,670 --> 01:06:47,238
Chunder!

913
01:06:51,112 --> 01:06:52,852
Pretty good landing.

914
01:06:54,158 --> 01:06:55,638
Whoa! Humans!

915
01:06:55,725 --> 01:06:57,248
I love humans!

916
01:06:57,335 --> 01:06:58,728
Two brothers,
their little sister,

917
01:06:58,815 --> 01:07:00,164
and an elderly couple.

918
01:07:00,251 --> 01:07:01,774
A couple?
Not a couple!

919
01:07:01,861 --> 01:07:04,037
Whoa! Looks like
I touched a nerve.

920
01:07:04,125 --> 01:07:06,039
Oh, look at this one.

921
01:07:06,127 --> 01:07:07,432
Hello. Ow!

922
01:07:07,519 --> 01:07:09,347
Toph, no! Bad Toph.

923
01:07:09,434 --> 01:07:11,088
We don't bite strangers.

924
01:07:12,220 --> 01:07:13,917
Great Spirit, excuse me.

925
01:07:14,004 --> 01:07:15,788
Did you just come from
that temple in the sky?

926
01:07:15,875 --> 01:07:17,268
I certainly did.

927
01:07:18,226 --> 01:07:20,750
It was my favorite hidey-hole
until that dark,

928
01:07:20,837 --> 01:07:23,231
yucky energy started
corrupting this whole place.

929
01:07:24,057 --> 01:07:26,973
Please, we need your help
getting up there.

930
01:07:27,060 --> 01:07:28,801
It's my duty to stop this.

931
01:07:29,324 --> 01:07:30,977
I'm the Avatar.

932
01:07:31,630 --> 01:07:34,851
Ooh, the Avatar.

933
01:07:35,373 --> 01:07:36,722
Let me have a squiz at you.

934
01:07:36,809 --> 01:07:39,638
Okay. Now with this eye.
And this eye.

935
01:07:39,725 --> 01:07:41,684
Mm-hmm. And this eye.
Don't forget this eye.

936
01:07:41,771 --> 01:07:44,295
Hey, hey, can we hurry up?
Every eye needs to have a squiz!

937
01:07:44,382 --> 01:07:45,514
Sniff check!

938
01:07:47,690 --> 01:07:49,953
Ooh, that's Avatar material
right there.

939
01:07:50,040 --> 01:07:52,434
Yes, it is. Oh!

940
01:07:52,521 --> 01:07:53,783
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

941
01:07:53,870 --> 01:07:56,177
It appears the universe
has brought us together

942
01:07:56,264 --> 01:07:58,179
for a very important mission...

943
01:07:58,744 --> 01:08:00,181
Ah?

944
01:08:00,268 --> 01:08:01,486
...to flee!

945
01:08:02,183 --> 01:08:03,662
Run for your lives!

946
01:08:03,749 --> 01:08:05,229
Wait, come back!

947
01:08:05,316 --> 01:08:06,839
You're going the wrong way!

948
01:08:06,926 --> 01:08:08,058
Stop!

949
01:08:08,537 --> 01:08:10,582
Please, Great Spirit,
both of our worlds are in danger!

950
01:08:10,669 --> 01:08:13,672
No, no, no, no, no, no.
I am not going back up there.

951
01:08:19,548 --> 01:08:22,681
Hmm. Well, when you
put it like that, it does make more sense.

952
01:08:23,813 --> 01:08:26,207
Upon reflection,
I've decided I shall help you

953
01:08:26,294 --> 01:08:27,643
and your human-y friends.

954
01:08:27,730 --> 01:08:30,080
What did he say?
Nice work, Momo.

955
01:08:30,167 --> 01:08:32,082
All right, in you go.

956
01:08:35,259 --> 01:08:36,826
By the way,
no eating anything you find

957
01:08:36,913 --> 01:08:38,523
in my teeth, as I'm
saving that for later.

958
01:08:39,176 --> 01:08:41,309
Ready, set, get steady and ret.

959
01:08:41,396 --> 01:08:44,268
One and a two
and a you know what to do.

960
01:08:44,355 --> 01:08:45,791
Blast off!

961
01:08:50,883 --> 01:08:53,364
I know we haven't known
each other very long, but...

962
01:08:53,451 --> 01:08:54,931
I love you!

963
01:08:55,018 --> 01:08:56,324
You don't have to say it back.

964
01:09:05,289 --> 01:09:06,899
Hey! You got your hair back!

965
01:09:06,986 --> 01:09:09,598
Why are my eyes teary?
Was I crying?

966
01:09:10,555 --> 01:09:12,427
No way! Look!

967
01:09:12,514 --> 01:09:13,950
What?
What is it?

968
01:09:14,037 --> 01:09:15,604
It's Republic City.

969
01:09:19,216 --> 01:09:21,871
We can't let him destroy
everything we built!

970
01:09:21,958 --> 01:09:23,307
We won't.

971
01:09:38,757 --> 01:09:39,845
Boomerang!

972
01:09:57,428 --> 01:09:58,908
Give me the staff, Tagah!

973
01:09:58,995 --> 01:10:01,563
I see I underestimated you,
Avatar.

974
01:10:01,650 --> 01:10:04,479
Your friends are stronger
than I thought.

975
01:10:04,566 --> 01:10:06,089
But you're too late.

976
01:10:14,402 --> 01:10:15,533
The Denied.

977
01:10:16,142 --> 01:10:18,928
You see?
I did what you wanted, Aang.

978
01:10:19,015 --> 01:10:21,409
I returned airbending
to the world.

979
01:10:23,019 --> 01:10:24,281
What's the plan?

980
01:10:24,542 --> 01:10:27,153
We'll deal with the Denied.
You have to get the staff.

981
01:10:27,893 --> 01:10:30,853
I will rebuild Jharana
on the ruins of our enemies,

982
01:10:30,940 --> 01:10:32,724
just as they did on ours.

983
01:10:32,811 --> 01:10:35,336
A new Air Empire will rise.

984
01:10:35,945 --> 01:10:37,555
Kill them all.

985
01:10:55,921 --> 01:10:57,793
We have to get
these people out of here.

986
01:11:14,244 --> 01:11:15,637
Oh, yeah!

987
01:11:22,861 --> 01:11:24,210
Tagah!

988
01:11:24,297 --> 01:11:25,473
Give it to me!

989
01:11:27,431 --> 01:11:28,737
This isn't the way!

990
01:11:28,824 --> 01:11:32,001
We can use the staff
to bring back balance, peace!

991
01:11:32,088 --> 01:11:34,090
You care so much
about your ideals

992
01:11:34,177 --> 01:11:35,961
that you let
your people die!

993
01:11:36,745 --> 01:11:39,356
I will do anything
to make sure they survive!

994
01:11:57,809 --> 01:11:59,681
My cabbages!
Not my cabbages!

995
01:12:05,382 --> 01:12:07,428
My cabbages!

996
01:12:08,080 --> 01:12:11,649
My cabbages!

997
01:12:24,053 --> 01:12:25,402
Don't do this.

998
01:12:25,489 --> 01:12:28,231
You have the power now.
You can decide how to use it.

999
01:12:28,318 --> 01:12:29,450
I'm not like you.

1000
01:12:29,537 --> 01:12:30,929
The world hasn't
been good to me.

1001
01:12:31,016 --> 01:12:32,627
The world is what we make it.

1002
01:12:33,062 --> 01:12:34,367
Get away from her!

1003
01:13:06,661 --> 01:13:07,923
Tagah, stop!

1004
01:13:13,232 --> 01:13:15,365
You betrayed me!
You betrayed our culture!

1005
01:13:15,452 --> 01:13:17,585
I gave you every chance
to see the truth!

1006
01:13:23,895 --> 01:13:25,941
Shouldn't you be
in the Fire Nation?

1007
01:13:28,160 --> 01:13:30,293
I'm fighting for the peace
of all nations!

1008
01:13:33,949 --> 01:13:36,038
Big talk from someone
who sits on a throne

1009
01:13:36,125 --> 01:13:37,561
built on a century of war!

1010
01:14:00,845 --> 01:14:04,153
I'm still the greatest
Earthbender in the world!

1011
01:14:28,177 --> 01:14:30,701
Oh, no.
I'm out of water.

1012
01:14:32,398 --> 01:14:34,531
We got ya!

1013
01:14:35,053 --> 01:14:37,534
And there's no Avatar
here to save you.

1014
01:14:39,101 --> 01:14:41,233
Sokka-Cycle!
Huh?

1015
01:14:44,976 --> 01:14:46,891
Let's see if
your fancy new bending

1016
01:14:46,978 --> 01:14:49,372
can beat some good old
nonbending know-how.

1017
01:14:56,640 --> 01:14:58,207
Bombs away!

1018
01:15:04,561 --> 01:15:06,345
You just got denied!

1019
01:15:07,695 --> 01:15:08,913
Whoa!

1020
01:15:15,572 --> 01:15:17,792
Let's go!
Good luck saving your city.

1021
01:15:19,271 --> 01:15:20,142
Huh?

1022
01:15:26,278 --> 01:15:28,672
We have to save
as many people as we can.

1023
01:15:47,256 --> 01:15:48,692
I know your pain.

1024
01:15:48,779 --> 01:15:50,476
I know what you've been through.

1025
01:15:51,434 --> 01:15:52,740
You don't know.

1026
01:15:53,697 --> 01:15:57,614
I watched as all of my brothers
and sisters were slaughtered.

1027
01:15:58,441 --> 01:16:02,097
When the Fire Nation
burned the Air Nomads to ash,

1028
01:16:02,184 --> 01:16:03,141
where were you?

1029
01:16:04,273 --> 01:16:05,448
You ran!

1030
01:16:26,251 --> 01:16:27,644
Tagah!

1031
01:16:37,610 --> 01:16:38,655
No!

1032
01:17:01,373 --> 01:17:06,465
The full power
of the Spirit World flows through me!

1033
01:17:16,214 --> 01:17:18,477
This is what strength
looks like!

1034
01:18:12,227 --> 01:18:14,185
You should've run away
like you did

1035
01:18:14,272 --> 01:18:17,145
all those years ago,
little Avatar.

1036
01:18:17,928 --> 01:18:18,973
I...

1037
01:18:20,148 --> 01:18:21,714
won't run.

1038
01:18:21,802 --> 01:18:25,936
Then at least you'll die
knowing you're not the last Airbender!

1039
01:19:03,147 --> 01:19:04,366
Aang!

1040
01:19:12,287 --> 01:19:13,244
No!

1041
01:19:44,188 --> 01:19:45,189
No.

1042
01:20:20,529 --> 01:20:22,618
We could've been brothers!

1043
01:20:23,227 --> 01:20:25,142
We could've done this together!

1044
01:20:25,229 --> 01:20:27,492
It didn't have to end like this!

1045
01:20:32,758 --> 01:20:34,456
It's Aang!
He's got the staff!

1046
01:20:34,543 --> 01:20:36,849
Yeah!
Kick his butt, Mega Aang!

1047
01:20:36,937 --> 01:20:38,547
No! Something's wrong!

1048
01:20:38,634 --> 01:20:40,505
The power is corrupting him!

1049
01:20:58,654 --> 01:21:00,961
I dreamt of bringing
the Air Nomads back

1050
01:21:01,048 --> 01:21:02,788
to the world
as peacekeepers.

1051
01:21:02,875 --> 01:21:04,616
They could have been
a beacon of light

1052
01:21:04,703 --> 01:21:06,053
for the world to follow.

1053
01:21:06,140 --> 01:21:07,706
But you ruined it!

1054
01:21:07,793 --> 01:21:10,144
You twisted my dream
into a nightmare!

1055
01:21:10,796 --> 01:21:14,626
Finally, you have the power
the Air Nomads need.

1056
01:21:14,713 --> 01:21:16,977
Maybe there is hope
for you after all.

1057
01:21:27,552 --> 01:21:30,555
Do it!
Use the staff!

1058
01:21:30,642 --> 01:21:33,254
Show me you have the strength
to bring our people back!

1059
01:21:34,385 --> 01:21:35,517
Do it!

1060
01:22:12,380 --> 01:22:13,511
<i>Aang.</i>

1061
01:22:16,210 --> 01:22:19,430
<i>You will do so many great things </i>
<i>as the Avatar,</i>

1062
01:22:20,127 --> 01:22:23,608
<i>but you must be prepared </i>
<i>to do what frightens you </i> <i>the most.</i>

1063
01:22:25,523 --> 01:22:30,093
<i>Your people, your home,</i>
<i>we are always with you.</i>

1064
01:22:46,675 --> 01:22:47,719
No.

1065
01:22:53,943 --> 01:22:55,205
No!

1066
01:23:18,620 --> 01:23:21,101
No! My power!

1067
01:23:27,107 --> 01:23:28,238
No.

1068
01:23:28,847 --> 01:23:29,979
No!

1069
01:23:39,554 --> 01:23:40,729
You fool!

1070
01:23:40,816 --> 01:23:42,165
Why?

1071
01:23:42,818 --> 01:23:44,602
Why did you break it?

1072
01:23:45,212 --> 01:23:47,605
We could have fixed everything.

1073
01:23:49,041 --> 01:23:51,392
We can't erase
the pain of the past.

1074
01:23:52,741 --> 01:23:54,134
We couldn't save them.

1075
01:23:54,221 --> 01:23:57,876
But it's our duty
to protect our people.

1076
01:23:58,225 --> 01:24:01,228
Not at the cost of betraying
everything they stood for.

1077
01:24:01,315 --> 01:24:02,533
No.

1078
01:24:03,186 --> 01:24:04,666
It's time to let go.

1079
01:24:05,928 --> 01:24:07,582
You have to forgive yourself.

1080
01:24:10,367 --> 01:24:12,413
I have to forgive myself too.

1081
01:24:21,552 --> 01:24:24,251
Air nomads are formed
from the mist.

1082
01:24:28,516 --> 01:24:32,172
We walk the world
for a moment in time.

1083
01:24:34,826 --> 01:24:38,830
Then we return
to the eternal wind.

1084
01:24:55,020 --> 01:24:56,457
Aang!

1085
01:25:00,112 --> 01:25:01,244
Hey, Katara.

1086
01:25:01,984 --> 01:25:03,028
Hey, Aang.

1087
01:25:05,640 --> 01:25:06,858
Seriously?

1088
01:25:06,945 --> 01:25:09,209
You do realize
you're falling, right?

1089
01:25:09,296 --> 01:25:11,646
Hey, if you ever get tired
of relying on Appa,

1090
01:25:11,733 --> 01:25:13,735
I could hook you up
with one of these babies.

1091
01:25:18,870 --> 01:25:20,872
I'll give you
the best friend discount!

1092
01:25:31,883 --> 01:25:33,015
These are pretty good!

1093
01:25:35,322 --> 01:25:37,628
<i>I don't know </i>
<i>if airbending will ever return,</i>

1094
01:25:38,325 --> 01:25:40,109
<i>but I know now</i>
<i>that the true power</i>

1095
01:25:40,196 --> 01:25:43,025
of the Air Nomads
was never their bending.

1096
01:25:43,678 --> 01:25:44,940
It was their values.

1097
01:25:45,854 --> 01:25:48,248
And that's a power
I can pass on to others.

1098
01:25:49,423 --> 01:25:52,730
Avatar Aang, you are
the true embodiment

1099
01:25:52,817 --> 01:25:54,297
of the Air Nomads.

1100
01:25:55,342 --> 01:25:58,301
Thank you for giving up
the power that I could not.

1101
01:25:59,171 --> 01:26:02,131
You give me hope for the future
of our culture.

1102
01:26:16,232 --> 01:26:17,842
It's amazing, isn't it?

1103
01:26:18,669 --> 01:26:21,411
The first new air temple
in centuries.

1104
01:26:22,760 --> 01:26:25,154
Republic City
is finally complete.

1105
01:26:29,332 --> 01:26:32,596
A city for all nations,
just like you promised.

1106
01:26:33,858 --> 01:26:36,252
I never could have done this
without you, Katara.

1107
01:26:37,645 --> 01:26:38,950
Hey, everybody.

1108
01:26:39,037 --> 01:26:40,778
Sorry I kept you all waiting.

1109
01:26:40,865 --> 01:26:42,519
Are you ready for our big trip?

1110
01:26:43,955 --> 01:26:47,307
As my new acolytes, you'll be
helping me preserve our culture

1111
01:26:47,394 --> 01:26:48,743
for future generations.

1112
01:26:49,700 --> 01:26:52,137
So, who wants
to search for artifacts

1113
01:26:52,224 --> 01:26:54,009
at an ancient
abandoned temple?

1114
01:26:54,139 --> 01:26:55,315
Yay.

1115
01:26:55,402 --> 01:26:56,881
I'm only going
to make sure you don't try

1116
01:26:56,968 --> 01:26:59,406
to release another
beefy old Airbender.

1117
01:26:59,493 --> 01:27:01,495
Yeah, I'm done
with bad boys.

1118
01:27:13,811 --> 01:27:15,944
Avatar Sonam told me
about this place.

1119
01:27:16,031 --> 01:27:18,512
So it's very possible
that no one's been here

1120
01:27:18,599 --> 01:27:20,035
in hundreds of years.

1121
01:27:21,515 --> 01:27:24,344
Oh! Is this
an Airbender relic?

1122
01:27:24,431 --> 01:27:26,041
I think that's just a rock.

1123
01:27:26,128 --> 01:27:27,651
But I love the enthusiasm.

1124
01:27:28,696 --> 01:27:30,437
Aw!

1125
01:27:33,918 --> 01:27:35,224
Keep your eyes open.

1126
01:27:35,311 --> 01:27:37,313
You never know what
we might discover here.

1127
01:27:38,836 --> 01:27:40,011
Woah!

1128
01:27:46,844 --> 01:27:48,411
I thought they were extinct.

1129
01:27:55,766 --> 01:27:57,159
I can't believe it.

1130
01:27:57,986 --> 01:27:59,640
The original Airbenders.

1131
01:28:06,951 --> 01:28:09,214
Aw, can I have one?

1132
01:28:10,564 --> 01:28:12,435
Appa, yip yip!

